 <LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy">
-    <h2>1. An overview of data protection</h2>
-    <p><strong>General information</strong></p>
-    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
-    
-    <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
-    <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
-    <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
-    
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <p>The DevTools Times is a demonstration news application. You can read articles without creating an account.</p>
+
+    <h2>Account details</h2>
+    <p>Sign-up and sign-in ask for a username and password only. Choose a username that does not identify you; we do not ask for your real name, email address, or profile details. Do not reuse a password from another service.</p>
+    <p>When you submit either form, these details are sent over HTTPS to our account service at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net</code>, hosted on Google Cloud. The service also receives network information, such as your IP address. Your credentials are sent to create an account or check your sign-in details, with no cookies or referring page attached by this application.</p>
+    <p>The forms do not log your credentials or save them to browser storage. The password field is cleared after each submission attempt. Your browser or password manager may offer to save credentials according to your own settings. This demo does not store the service's returned authentication token or keep you signed in.</p>
+    <p>The account service is separate from this website's source code. Its credential storage, retention period, and deletion process have not been verified here. Do not submit personal or sensitive credentials to this demo.</p>
+
+    <h2>Scripts, fonts, and external content</h2>
+    <p>The shared page layout does not load third-party analytics, advertising scripts, or remote fonts. There is no analytics opt-in to complete, and browsing does not require marketing consent.</p>
+    <p>Some articles include externally hosted images or embedded content. Loading that content can reveal network information to its host. Our document referrer policy prevents sending the referring page address. Following an external link takes you to a site with its own privacy practices.</p>
+
+    <h2>Reading list and essential storage</h2>
+    <p>Saving an article stores its identifier in a server-side reading list associated with a session cookie. An empty reading list is not created just because you visit. You can remove saved articles using their bookmark controls; clearing this site's cookies disconnects your browser from its saved list, but does not itself delete server-side records.</p>
+    <p>Website hosting and the account service may process request metadata to deliver their services. This application does not define their logging or retention settings.</p>
+
+    <h2>Questions</h2>
+    <p>For information about the publisher, see the <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}legal/imprint`}>Imprint</a>. Backend retention and account deletion arrangements need to be confirmed with the operator before this demo is used with real personal data.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
